# TradingView Follow Line STC MACD EMA

## Source
- Source: [[sources/tradingview-mechanical-strategy-scripts]]
- Page / Timestamp: TradingView script `FLI + STC + MACD + EMA Strategy v1`, author handle `wikitrader1`, open-source strategy, accessed 2026-05-22, page shows Apr 3, https://www.tradingview.com/script/xlNwG5Ho-FLI-STC-MACD-EMA-Strategy-v1/

## Mechanics

### Entry
Use H1 baseline:

- Compute Follow Line Indicator from Bollinger Band structure with ATR filtering enabled.
- Compute Schaff Trend Cycle.
- Compute MACD line, signal, and histogram.
- Compute EMA bias, default EMA(200).
- P2 baseline uses Balanced mode: Follow Line bullish flip plus at least two enabled bullish confirmations.
- Long confirmations: STC bullish threshold cross or positive slope, MACD bullish cross or positive histogram slope, close > EMA(200).
- Short confirmations: Follow Line bearish flip plus at least two bearish confirmations from STC, MACD, and close < EMA(200).
- Enter on confirmed bar close only.

### Exit
- Source visible text is entry/alert focused and does not publish full native exits.
- V5 baseline exits: opposite Follow Line flip, ATR stop/target, and time exit.
- Close long on bearish Follow Line flip or MACD bearish cross; close short on bullish Follow Line flip or MACD bullish cross.

### Stop Loss
- Initial stop = ATR(14) * 1.5 from entry.
- Target = ATR(14) * 2.5 from entry.
- Time exit after 36 H1 bars if no stop/target/opposite flip occurs.

### Position Sizing
V5 default: fixed-risk $1,000 for P2 baseline, one position per symbol/magic.

### Zusatzliche Filter
- Freeze confirmation mode to Balanced for P2; do not optimize entry mode inside a single run.
- EMA bias defaults to price above/below EMA(200).
- Disable debug/alert-only pathways; EA trades only closed-bar confirmed signals.

## Concepts (what kind of strategy is this)
- [[concepts/trend-following]] - Follow Line and EMA define directional trend.
- [[concepts/momentum-confirmation]] - STC and MACD confirm timing.
- [[concepts/confluence-filter]] - Balanced mode requires multiple confirmations.

